[section, $md:
    # Builder packages

    The selected project builder supplies packages tied to its artefact model.
    This keeps browser and rendering APIs out of the core language.

    The HTML builder provides static URLs through `@web/site`, binding-backed
    runtime drawing through `@web/canvas`, WebGL2 rendering through `@web/graphics`
    and live browser state through `@web/page`. The universal `@html` and
    `@styles` Core packages are available under every builder and documented in
    @../core/ (Core packages). The
    @../../progress/packages-and-builders (packages and builders progress matrix)
    records current support and accepted next gaps.

    ## Package pages

    - @./canvas/ (@web/canvas)
    - @./graphics/ (@web/graphics)
    - @./site/ (@web/site)
    - @./page/ (@web/page)
]

